#: includes/mcp/class-ppcart-mcp-abilities.php:46
msgid "PublishPress plugin actions."
msgstr ""

#: includes/mcp/class-ppcart-mcp-abilities.php:64
msgid "Discover Cart features"
msgstr ""

#: includes/mcp/class-ppcart-mcp-abilities.php:65
msgid "Find native Cart screen and editor scopes, available read/write actions, edition boundaries and required capabilities. Discovery does not grant permission; every action rechecks native capabilities and individual objects."
msgstr ""

#: includes/mcp/class-ppcart-mcp-abilities.php:73
msgid "Get Cart store settings"
msgstr ""

#: includes/mcp/class-ppcart-mcp-abilities.php:74
msgid "Read store currency, company, account page and transactional email settings. Returns exact option identifiers, native stored values, defaults, accepted JSON types, choices and a revision. Read this before changing settings; checkbox writes use JSON booleans, not strings."
msgstr ""

#: includes/mcp/class-ppcart-mcp-abilities.php:84
msgid "Update Cart store settings"
msgstr ""

#: includes/mcp/class-ppcart-mcp-abilities.php:85
msgid "Patch Cart store settings and transactional emails using identifiers and the revision from get-settings. Omitted settings are preserved. All changes are validated before writing. Use dry_run=true to preview native sanitized values. Does not accept credentials or payment gateway operations."
msgstr ""

#: includes/mcp/class-ppcart-mcp-abilities.php:99
msgid "Cart secure product downloads"
msgstr ""

#: includes/mcp/class-ppcart-mcp-abilities.php:100
msgid "Read native file fields and revision before replacing the ordered rows list. Retained file_id values preserve hidden source URLs and omitted properties. New sources require an editable attachment_id uploaded through Cart secure uploads and upload_files capability. No customer access keys, signed links or source URLs are returned. Native Pro enables expiry/hidden controls. dry_run previews without changing files or access."
msgstr ""

#: includes/mcp/class-ppcart-mcp-abilities.php:115
msgid "Cart product integration rules"
msgstr ""

#: includes/mcp/class-ppcart-mcp-abilities.php:116
msgid "Read active native services, triggers, field choices and revision. Set replaces ordered rows; retain row_id to preserve credentials and omitted fields internally, or omit row_id for a new rule. Requires manage_options and product edit permission. User rules also check user administration capabilities and reject privileged roles. Native Pro dependencies govern Pro services. dry_run never executes rules. Read mapping_sources for approved order fields and declared non-password custom fields. Mappings use destination/source pairs; arbitrary metadata and secret fields are rejected. Refresh discovery when provider choices expire. Authentication headers and credentials stay in native administration and are never returned."
msgstr ""

#: includes/mcp/class-ppcart-mcp-abilities.php:127
msgid "Cart product purchase notifications"
msgstr ""

#: includes/mcp/class-ppcart-mcp-abilities.php:128
msgid "Read native notification fields and revision, or replace the complete ordered notification list for an editable product. Required fields are notification_name, subject, message and send_to (enter, purchaser, admin). Explicit recipients require send_to_email. Checkbox writes are booleans. Empty optional strings use native nulls. dry_run previews without saving or sending mail; configuring notifications never sends mail immediately."
msgstr ""

#: includes/mcp/class-ppcart-mcp-abilities.php:138
msgid "Get Cart product settings"
msgstr ""

#: includes/mcp/class-ppcart-mcp-abilities.php:139
msgid "Read a product configuration, native field labels, exact types, accepted choices and revision. Requires permission to edit this specific product. Does not return gateway secrets or download tokens."
msgstr ""

#: includes/mcp/class-ppcart-mcp-abilities.php:150
msgid "Update Cart product settings"
msgstr ""

#: includes/mcp/class-ppcart-mcp-abilities.php:151
msgid "Patch product appearance, availability, stock, sale and confirmation settings. Use the exact identifiers and revision from get-product-settings. Preview with dry_run=true. Preserves omitted fields. Payment plan, coupon and external payment lifecycles are separate operations."
msgstr ""

#: includes/mcp/class-ppcart-mcp-abilities.php:159
msgid "Get Cart payment plans"
msgstr ""

#: includes/mcp/class-ppcart-mcp-abilities.php:160
msgid "Read payment plan rows, native field definitions, exact accepted types and revision for a product. Gateway-generated identifiers are not editable. Use this before set-payment-plans."
msgstr ""

#: includes/mcp/class-ppcart-mcp-abilities.php:171
msgid "Set Cart payment plans"
msgstr ""

#: includes/mcp/class-ppcart-mcp-abilities.php:172
msgid "Replace the ordered payment-plan list for a product using its revision. Every row needs a unique option_id; omitted fields on retained plan IDs are preserved. Omitted rows are removed. Native plan types include one-time (empty string), recurring, pwyw and free. At least one plan must remain visible. dry_run=true validates without contacting gateways. Saving runs native Stripe synchronization; an unconfirmed gateway result must not be automatically retried."
msgstr ""

#: includes/mcp/class-ppcart-mcp-abilities.php:188
msgid "Find Cart products, orders and subscriptions"
msgstr ""

#: includes/mcp/class-ppcart-mcp-abilities.php:189
msgid "Find Cart record IDs by kind and title search with bounded pagination. Results are filtered by native record permissions. Use get-record for order/subscription details or get-product-settings for product configuration. This action never changes order or payment state."
msgstr ""

#: includes/mcp/class-ppcart-mcp-abilities.php:197
msgid "Get a Cart record"
msgstr ""

#: includes/mcp/class-ppcart-mcp-abilities.php:198
msgid "Read a known product, order or subscription using its kind and ID. Orders include local payment status, amount, refund totals and customer name/email when permitted. No payment credentials, receipt tokens, download links or raw gateway responses are returned."
msgstr ""

#: includes/mcp/class-ppcart-mcp-abilities.php:212
msgid "Create a Cart catalog record"
msgstr ""

#: includes/mcp/class-ppcart-mcp-abilities.php:213
msgid "Create a Cart product draft or another supported catalog kind. Requires native create permission; publishing/private status also requires publish permission. Uses WordPress content sanitization. Defaults to draft. dry_run=true previews without creating a post. Configure product settings and payment plans separately after creation."
msgstr ""

#: includes/mcp/class-ppcart-mcp-abilities.php:222
msgid "Update a Cart catalog record"
msgstr ""

#: includes/mcp/class-ppcart-mcp-abilities.php:223
msgid "Patch title, content, excerpt, slug, featured_image_id (zero removes it) or publication status of an editable Cart catalog record. Read get-record and supply its revision first. Preserves omitted post fields and product configuration. dry_run=true previews without writing. Cannot edit orders or subscription state."
msgstr ""

#: includes/mcp/class-ppcart-mcp-abilities.php:239
msgid "Find product categories and tags"
msgstr ""

#: includes/mcp/class-ppcart-mcp-abilities.php:240
msgid "Create a product category or tag"
msgstr ""

#: includes/mcp/class-ppcart-mcp-abilities.php:241
msgid "Update a product category or tag"
msgstr ""

#: includes/mcp/class-ppcart-mcp-abilities.php:242
msgid "Get product category or tag assignments"
msgstr ""

#: includes/mcp/class-ppcart-mcp-abilities.php:243
msgid "Preview product term deletion scope"
msgstr ""

#: includes/mcp/class-ppcart-mcp-abilities.php:244
msgid "Delete a product category or tag"
msgstr ""

#: includes/mcp/class-ppcart-mcp-abilities.php:245
msgid "Set product category or tag assignments"
msgstr ""

#: includes/mcp/class-ppcart-mcp-abilities.php:251
msgid "Use taxonomy category or tag. Lists are paginated. Term updates and replacing a product term_ids list require the revision returned by the corresponding read. Writes support dry_run. Assignment validates every term before writing and preserves the other taxonomy. For deletion, first get-product-term-deletion and supply its scope revision; all affected products and reparented child terms require native permissions. Native taxonomy and product permissions apply."
msgstr ""

#: includes/mcp/class-ppcart-mcp-abilities.php:265
msgid "Get Cart monthly overview"
msgstr ""

#: includes/mcp/class-ppcart-mcp-abilities.php:266
msgid "Read the native Monthly Overview dashboard metrics for the current site month: order counts and amounts, subscription statistics and plan statistics. Uses the same native calculations as the dashboard widget."
msgstr ""

#: includes/mcp/class-ppcart-mcp-abilities.php:275
msgid "Resend an order confirmation"
msgstr ""

#: includes/mcp/class-ppcart-mcp-abilities.php:276
msgid "Read get-order-details and supply its revision. Sends the native paid-order confirmation to native configured recipients. Requires financial and related object/user permissions. dry_run sends nothing. Not idempotent; check delivery before retrying."
msgstr ""

#: includes/mcp/class-ppcart-mcp-abilities.php:287
msgid "Inspect or reconcile a payment operation"
msgstr ""

#: includes/mcp/class-ppcart-mcp-abilities.php:288
msgid "Read uncertain operation state without provider IDs or credentials. Resolve requires its revision and a confirmed native outcome after provider synchronization. It cannot discard an unknown result or retry a charge/refund. dry_run does not release the lock."
msgstr ""

#: includes/mcp/class-ppcart-mcp-abilities.php:301
msgid "Refund a Cart order"
msgstr ""

#: includes/mcp/class-ppcart-mcp-abilities.php:302
msgid "Issue a native order refund. Read get-record first and supply its revision. Amount is a positive decimal string using a dot, at most the remaining refundable balance. dry_run=true previews locally without contacting a gateway. Restocking also requires edit access to the product. A gateway action cannot be rolled back; do not automatically retry an unconfirmed result."
msgstr ""

#: includes/mcp/class-ppcart-mcp-abilities.php:311
msgid "Cancel a Cart subscription"
msgstr ""

#: includes/mcp/class-ppcart-mcp-abilities.php:312
msgid "Cancel a subscription immediately or at period end using its persisted gateway identity. Read get-record first and supply its revision. dry_run=true previews locally without contacting the gateway. Does not issue a refund. Do not automatically retry an unconfirmed result."
msgstr ""

#: includes/mcp/class-ppcart-mcp-abilities.php:322
msgid "Pause or resume a Cart subscription"
msgstr ""

#: includes/mcp/class-ppcart-mcp-abilities.php:323
msgid "Read the subscription and provide its revision. Uses the persisted gateway identity/mode and native ownership rules, in addition to Cart payment and object permissions. dry_run validates locally without a gateway call. Pausing requires active/trialing/past_due; resuming requires paused. Inspect unconfirmed remote outcomes before retrying."
msgstr ""

#: includes/mcp/class-ppcart-mcp-abilities.php:335
msgid "Cart order download access"
msgstr ""

#: includes/mcp/class-ppcart-mcp-abilities.php:336
msgid "Read authorized order download access without customer keys, signed links or sources. Updates and revocation require its revision and an access row belonging to that order. downloads_remaining is a nonnegative integer or null for unlimited; download_expires is native site-local YYYY-MM-DD HH:MM:SS or null for no expiry. dry_run previews without changing access. Native order and payment permissions apply."
msgstr ""

#: includes/mcp/class-ppcart-mcp-abilities.php:346
msgid "Upload a secure Cart file"
msgstr ""

#: includes/mcp/class-ppcart-mcp-abilities.php:347
msgid "Upload a binary file of at most 2 MiB (or the lower WordPress limit) as strict base64 with its lowercase SHA-256 checksum and plain filename. Requires upload_files and product edit access. Uses WordPress MIME checks and the native secure upload directory. Returns only attachment identity, MIME type, size and checksum. Assign attachment_id using set-product-files. Do not upload credentials or automatically retry an unconfirmed upload."
msgstr ""

#: includes/mcp/class-ppcart-mcp-abilities.php:357
msgid "Cart service setup"
msgstr ""

#: includes/mcp/class-ppcart-mcp-abilities.php:358
msgid "Get authenticated native WordPress settings destinations for gateway credentials and integration authorization. Does not accept, read or return credentials, bearer URLs or authorization tokens. Requires manage_options."
msgstr ""

#: includes/mcp/class-ppcart-mcp-abilities.php:367
msgid "Cart Stripe checkout experience"
msgstr ""

#: includes/mcp/class-ppcart-mcp-abilities.php:368
msgid "Choose classic, element or hosted using the native combined selector. Read its revision first. dry_run previews without changing options or contacting Stripe. Hosted checkout does not support order bumps or one-click upsells/downsells. Credentials are configured in the native settings screen."
msgstr ""

#: includes/mcp/class-ppcart-mcp-abilities.php:377
msgid "Export Cart customer reports"
msgstr ""

#: includes/mcp/class-ppcart-mcp-abilities.php:378
msgid "Export CSV pages of orders, subscriptions or contacts. Order exports include customer names, email, phone, address and purchase amounts. Requires native report/export capabilities and read/edit access to every included record. Optional order/subscription filters: inclusive from/to dates, product_id and email. Contacts support email only, with at most 1,000 contributing orders per response. Default 50, maximum 100 rows and 1 MiB per response. Follow next_page; concurrent edits can change pages. No gateway/receipt tokens, arbitrary custom fields or source URLs. Spreadsheet formulas are escaped."
msgstr ""

#: includes/mcp/class-ppcart-mcp-abilities.php:388
msgid "Cart catalog lifecycle"
msgstr ""

#: includes/mcp/class-ppcart-mcp-abilities.php:389
msgid "Read a catalog lifecycle revision before duplicating a product, moving a catalog record to trash, restoring it or permanently deleting a trashed record. Orders and subscriptions are excluded. Native object permissions apply. Duplication also validates copied integration grants. dry_run validates without writes. Do not retry an unconfirmed mutation."
msgstr ""

#: includes/mcp/class-ppcart-mcp-abilities.php:400
msgid "Cart manual order administration"
msgstr ""

#: includes/mcp/class-ppcart-mcp-abilities.php:401
msgid "Read/update native order contact, address, account and administrative status fields. Updates require a current revision; omitted fields are preserved. Stripe status is locked. create-manual-order records an offline/COD order using native product plan pricing; it does not charge a payment or create a gateway subscription. Native status/create hooks can run notifications and integrations. All related user/product/subscription permissions and existing integration grant policies are checked. dry_run validates locally without saving, sending email or contacting providers. Use refund-order for actual refunds, rather than a bookkeeping status change."
msgstr ""

#: includes/mcp/class-ppcart-mcp-abilities.php:412
msgid "Send a Cart transactional test email"
msgstr ""

#: includes/mcp/class-ppcart-mcp-abilities.php:413
msgid "Send a native transactional template test to configured administrator/test recipients, using synthetic customer data without reading real orders or charging payments. Requires manage_options and native financial permission. dry_run=true lists current native template types and sends nothing. Sending is not idempotent; check delivery before retrying."
msgstr ""

#: includes/mcp/class-ppcart-mcp-abilities.php:424
msgid "Cart native Stripe synchronization"
msgstr ""

#: includes/mcp/class-ppcart-mcp-abilities.php:425
msgid "Read the affected local scope and revision before refreshing a stored Stripe order or subscription through native synchronization. Requires financial and related record/product/user permissions, including native order creation permissions for invoice synchronization. Uses persisted gateway mode; accepts no provider identifiers or credentials. dry_run performs no network calls or writes. Synchronization can run native status effects; inspect unconfirmed outcomes before retrying."
msgstr ""

